# Commands & Scripts

## Root Scripts (run from repo root)
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `pnpm dev` | Start backend (port 4000) + web (port 3000) in dev mode |
| `pnpm desktop` | Start backend (port 4000) + desktop (Vite on port 5173) in dev mode |
| `pnpm build` | Build all apps and packages (outputs to `.next/` and `dist/`) |
| `pnpm lint` | Lint all apps and packages with ESLint (flat config) |
| `pnpm format` | Format all `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.md` files with Prettier (defaults) |
| `pnpm check-types` | Type-check all apps and packages |
| `pnpm test` | Run all Vitest tests |
| `pnpm db:push` | Push Prisma schema to SQLite (`apps/backend/data/farm.db`) |
| `pnpm db:studio` | Open Prisma Studio for DB inspection |

## Turbo Filters
Run a specific app or package in isolation:
- `pnpm turbo dev --filter=backend` — start only the backend
- `pnpm turbo dev --filter=web` — start only the web dashboard
- `pnpm turbo dev --filter=desktop` — start only the desktop app
- `pnpm turbo test --filter=@bot-ville/core` — test only the core package
- `pnpm turbo test --filter=@bot-ville/memory` — test only the memory package
- `pnpm turbo build --filter=@bot-ville/shared` — build only the shared package
- `pnpm turbo lint --filter=backend` — lint only the backend

## Prisma Commands
Run from `apps/backend/`:
- `npx prisma db push` — push schema to SQLite (creates `data/farm.db` if missing)
- `npx prisma studio` — open Prisma Studio GUI
- `npx prisma generate` — regenerate Prisma client after schema changes

## Dev Server Ports
| Service | Port | URL |
|---|---|---|
| Backend API | 4000 | `http://localhost:4000` |
| Web Dashboard | 3000 | `http://localhost:3000` |
| Desktop Vite Dev | 5173 | `http://localhost:5173` |
| WebSocket | 4000 | `ws://localhost:4000/ws` |

## Turbo Pipeline (`turbo.json`)
- `build` — depends on `^build` (builds deps first); inputs include `.env*`; outputs: `.next/**`, `dist/**`
- `lint` — depends on `^lint`
- `check-types` — depends on `^check-types`
- `dev` — persistent, no cache
- `test` — depends on `^build`, no cache
- `package` — depends on `build`; outputs: `release/**`

## Notes
- `pnpm dev` starts both backend + web in parallel via Turbo (`--filter=backend --filter=web`)
- `pnpm desktop` starts both backend + desktop in parallel via Turbo (`--filter=backend --filter=desktop`)
- The Electron main process (`apps/desktop/src/main/main.ts`) also spawns the Next.js web app as a child process on port 3000
